<title>INDIA: India SPIC 1996/97 net higher.</title>
<headline>India SPIC 1996/97 net higher.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net Profit		726.2	vs     811.1</p>
<p>    Turnover	     18,321.8	vs  18,428.8</p>
<p>    Dividend (in rupees)    3.0	vs	 3.0</p>
<p>    Interest and fin.     975.5	vs     937.6</p>
<p>    Gross profit	  2,220.5	vs   2,109.6</p>
<p>    Depreciation	    472.8	vs     360.9</p>
<p>    Tax			  46.0	vs	nil</p>
<p>Note: India's Southern Petrochemical Industries Corporation Ltd (SPIC), involved in chemicals and fertilizer, said previous years figures had been &quot;regrouped/recast&quot; wherever necessary to confirm with the current year.</p>
<p>The firm said it will increase its authorised capital to 3.0 billion rupees from 2.3 billion rupees. SPIC said it had created an additional 7.0 million preference shares of 100 rupees each. The company will hold its annual general meeting on August 27.</p>
<p>-- Bombay equities desk +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
